------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

CryoMap depends on third-party open-source software that is downloaded at
install time (via pnpm) and is not redistributed in this repository. A complete
inventory of dependency licenses is in docs/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md. The vast
majority are MIT-, ISC-, BSD-, or Apache-2.0-licensed. The following components
carry attribution or notice terms worth calling out:

- caniuse-lite (CC-BY-4.0) — browser-support data used at build time by
  Browserslist. Data © caniuse.com contributors, used under the Creative
  Commons Attribution 4.0 International license.

- dompurify (dual-licensed MPL-2.0 OR Apache-2.0) — used under Apache-2.0.

- axe-core, lightningcss (MPL-2.0) — used unmodified as build/test tooling;
  their source and MPL-2.0 terms travel with the published packages.

- sharp → libvips (@img/sharp-libvips-*, LGPL-3.0-or-later) — an optional,
  platform-specific native image library used unmodified for Next.js image
  optimization.

- Geist and Geist Mono fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1) — © Vercel, loaded via
  next/font.

Each dependency's full license text ships inside its own package under
node_modules/<package>. This NOTICE file does not modify the terms of any
third-party license.
